<urn:atm:triage:finding/R2B-RBP-F002>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "R2B-RBP-F002" ;
  triage:title "PreparedCheck.criteria is BTreeMap<String, BTreeSet<String>>, so question ids and choice labels are raw strings. question_criteria, criteria_from_object and criteria_from_array (check.rs:245-329) re-validate and re-derive them from the payload bytes. parse_outcome (check.rs:226, 228) later converts them to QuestionId and ChoiceId via try_from and response_label. The typed map already exists on PayloadBundle::question_choices(). Recommendation: Build the expected-answer map from request.payload().question_choices() (QuestionId/ChoiceId) and have parse_outcome compare typed ids. Keep only the Jev-specific shape checks (object or array questions, at least 2 criteria) that the bundle does not cover." ;
  triage:description "PreparedCheck.criteria is BTreeMap<String, BTreeSet<String>>, so question ids and choice labels are raw strings. question_criteria, criteria_from_object and criteria_from_array (check.rs:245-329) re-validate and re-derive them from the payload bytes. parse_outcome (check.rs:226, 228) later converts them to QuestionId and ChoiceId via try_from and response_label. The typed map already exists on PayloadBundle::question_choices(). Recommendation: Build the expected-answer map from request.payload().question_choices() (QuestionId/ChoiceId) and have parse_outcome compare typed ids. Keep only the Jev-specific shape checks (object or array questions, at least 2 criteria) that the bundle does not cover." ;
